---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import site from "../data/site.json";
---

<Layout>
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-14 pb-10">
        <h1
            class="mb-4 text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-none md:text-7xl"
        >
            Machine Learning Reading Program
        </h1>
        <p
            class="mb-4 text-sm font-medium tracking-wide text-text-muted uppercase"
        >
            {site.university}
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
            <a
                href="/join"
                class="inline-block rounded-md bg-text px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-cream no-underline transition-opacity hover:opacity-80"
            >
                Join the Program
            </a>
            <a
                href="/about"
                class="inline-block rounded-md border border-divider px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-text no-underline transition-colors hover:bg-cream-dark"
            >
                Learn More
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
        <div class="h-px bg-divider"></div>
    </div>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">What Is MLRP?</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-text-muted">
            <!-- <p>
                    The Machine Learning Reading Program (MLRP) is a student-run
                    initiative at the University of Washington that connects
                    undergraduates with graduate and postdoctoral researchers
                    through guided reading and discussion of machine learning
                    research papers.
                </p> -->
            <p>
                The Machine Learning Reading Program (MLRP) is a student-run
                initiative at the University of Washington that connects
                undergraduates with graduate and postdoctoral mentors to read
                and discuss machine learning research papers.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
        <div class="h-px bg-divider"></div>
    </div>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">How Does It Work?</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-text-muted">
            <p>
                Undergraduates are paired with a graduate or postdoctoral mentor
                to read and discuss approximately eight machine learning-related
                research papers over the course of a quarter.
            </p>
            <p>
                Research papers are selected collaboratively by mentors and
                mentees. Pairs meet weekly at a flexible, mutually agreed-upon
                time throughout the quarter.
            </p>
            <p>
                At the end of the quarter, undergraduates give a short
                presentation on one or more of their favorite papers.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
        <div class="h-px bg-divider"></div>
    </div>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">Who Should Apply?</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-text-muted">
            <p>
                The program is <strong>open to all undergraduates</strong>,
                regardless of major. Students from any academic or personal
                background are welcome, as long as they bring curiosity about
                machine learning.
            </p>
            <p>
                Even if you're not interested in pure machine learning, you are
                still encouraged to apply. We aim to have mentors across a <strong
                    >wide range of fields</strong
                >, from robotics to natural language processing, AI for science,
                and more.
            </p>
            <p>
                While some familiarity with calculus, linear algebra, and
                probability may be helpful, there are no formal prerequisites
                for participating in the program.
            </p>
            <p>
                The program may be especially useful for students who are
                considering graduate school or a career in research.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
        <div class="h-px bg-divider"></div>
    </div>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">Why MLRP?</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-text-muted">
            <p>
                Many undergrads interested in machine learning eventually ask
                the question: how do I get started in research? The typical
                advice they get is to take courses, but the knowledge gained
                from courses is only part of what's required. The ability to
                read, engage, and keep up with current research papers, an
                essential skill for doing research, is often overlooked. MLRP
                aims to bridge this gap by connecting undergrads with machine
                learning researchers to build this skill.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section> -->
</Layout>
